# Drive My Car, intro (figure 77.1)
# Rhythm from Pollack's count row: eighth-note slots, an eighth pickup (A on the "and"). The
# bass enters on beat 3 of bar 1 and its last D ties over into bar 2; the guitar's D on the "and"
# of 4 ties over the downbeat too. His accent marks (>) fall on those two D's (the "and" of 4 in
# bar 1, the "and" of 1 in bar 2). The drum fill starts on beat 3 of bar 2.
# The third bar is the downbeat of the verse he shows after the double bar ("Verse ...", bass D,
# "Cymbals!"). Harmonic envelope: D major throughout (C- and F-naturals are bluesy).
#? Guitar octaves: the F on beat 3 of bar 1 is taken as the "bent high note" (F5); it may be another note, or the F may sit below the A.
#? Bass octave guessed (A2 up to D3, D3 into the verse).
key D

